  "verbalization": "Heparin, Bovine is implicated in the development of Pulmonary Embolism (disease) through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the indication of Purpura Fulminans. This connection is supported by the shared indication of Purpura Fulminans with Enoxaparin and Adomiparin, as well as with Ardeparin, which in turn is linked to Pulmonary Embolism. The evidence suggests that Heparin, Bovine may exert a therapeutic or pathophysiological effect that is indirectly linked to the development of Pulmonary Embolism through its role in the induction of Purpura Fulminans. The presence of multiple related compounds—Heparin, Enoxaparin, and Adomiparin—indicates a potential family of drugs that may share similar mechanisms of action or pathophysiological effects, contributing to the observed relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in assessing the reusability of Heparin for treating Pulmonary Embolism.",
